 and 6cm to the superior resection margins  The represenative cross section prepared  closest to the tumor  The inferior margin in cassette A  the anterior margin in B  posterior margin in C  the superior margin in D  the medial resection margin in E  Two representative sections from the different portions of the tumor are in cassettes F and G  A section of a separate nodular lesion present in the lateral portion of the breast parenchma submitted in cassette H  A piece of nipple submitted in cassette I  A REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm round shaped tan yellow soft tissue is present in the axillary tail possibly lymph node  Representative sections submitted in cassettes J and K  A REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm well circumscribed yellow soft tissue is present in the axillary tail  Two cross sections submitted in cassettes L and M  One representative section of each lymph node ranging in size from REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1cm to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm submitted in cassettes N through Q  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  additional lymph node right axilla  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm lymph node  bisected  and entirely submitted in cassette R  Resident  SONER ALTIOK  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Janey Sue Pratt  M D  Neil G Harness  M D  PART A  BREAST  RIGHT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY PART B  LYMPH NODE  RIGHT  ADDITIONAL AXILLARY TISSUE    E , Yes.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  27 REMOVED_MONTH 96 ACCESSIONED ON  27 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 09 31 CLINICAL DATA  FNA showed ductal carcinoma of right breast                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   MASTECTOMY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  MICROPAPILLARY TYPE  REMOVED_DATE CM  GRADE 2  INVADING LYMPHATIC VESSELS  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  SEE NOTE  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLA   METASTATIC CARCINOMA IN 2 OF 14 LYMPH NODES  SEE NOTE  BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protien  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  05 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 15 53 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number are three parts  Labeled  right breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 5cm breast with an irregular shape REMOVED_DATE x 15 0cm fragment of skin containing an unremarkable REMOVED_DATE x 1 3cm nipple  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 1cm ill defined white to tan firm mass on the lateral aspect of the breast 0 3cm from the closest  anterior  superficial  resection margin and 2 0cm from the closest deep resection margin  Immediately lateral to the main mass is an ill defined REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm white  fibrous area abutting the anterior  superficial resection margin  The remaining breast parenchyma is mostly fatty and unremarkable  Section code  A B and C  tumor with closest anterior superficial resection margin D  tumor with skin E  tumor  br report_end  , No.
