ablished and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Atul Kumar Bhan  M D  Signed On  25 REMOVED_MONTH 03 at 16 24 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left axillary nodal contents   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm aggregate of fibroadipose tissue  Multiple lymph nodes are identified  and are submitted as follows  A  One 1 5cm lymph node  trisected  B  One 1 8cm lymph node  trisected  C  One 1 2cm lymph node  bisected  D  One 1 5cm lymph node  trisected  E  One 1 3cm lymph node  trisected  F  One 0 9cm lymph node  bisected  G  One 0 8cm lymph node  bisected  H  One 0 9cm lymph node  bisected  I  One 0 5cm lymph node  submitted whole  as well as several potential lymph nodes  submitted whole  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast   is a 16 x 15 x 4cm simple mastectomy specimen with an anterior skin ellipse measuring REMOVED_DATE x 5cm  containing a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm nipple  There is a stitch on the skin ellipse designated by the surgeon as 12 o clock  There is a 4cm curvilinear  well healed scar  1 5cm lateral to the nipple on the skin surface  The skin surface and the nipple are unremarkable  The specimen is inked as follows  anterior blue  posterior black  Serial sectioning reveals a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm hemorrhagic  cavitary area  consistent with a prior biopsy site  This area is located 1 5cm from the closest posterior margin  and 0 9cm from the skin surface  deep to the scar  The surrounding breast parenchyma demonstrates an area of increased  irregular  rubbery to firm fibrosis  located 3cm away from the biopsy cavity  and measuring 3 x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm  This area of fibrosis is located 0 1cm from the posterior margin  The remainder of the breast parenchyma is predominantly fatty and focally fibrotic and contains no discrete masses  The area of the axillary region is examined for lymph no