Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Updated Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  MS 08  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CASE  MS 08  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  Date Taken  REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit  MGH Inpatient Path Subspecialty Service  Breast 2 Results To  BARBARA LYNN SMITH  M D  Frozen Section Pathologist  Chin Lee Wu  M D  Frozen Section Resident  Omer Yilmaz  M D   Ph D  Signed Out by  Melinda J Lerwill  M D             Addended Report             Reason for Addendum  1  Additional Immunohistochemistry Results Reason for Addendum  2  Additional Fluorescence In Situ Hybridization  FISH  Results CLINICAL DATA  Left breast CA  FINAL DIAGNOSIS  LYMPH NODE  LEFT AXILLA  SENTINEL   EXCISION  A FEW ISOLATED TUMOR CELLS   3 CELLS  IN 1 OF 1 LYMPH NODE  SEE NOTE AND TABLE  1  NOTE  The isolated tumor cells are only identified on the cytokeratin 7 immunostained level  Immunostains for cytokeratin  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  3 CAM REMOVED_DATE and pankeratin on two additional levels were also examined  TABLE OF PATHOLOGIC FINDINGS   1 SENTINEL LYMPH NODES TOTAL NUMBER OF POSITIVE LYMPH NODES  1 TOTAL NUMBER OF LYMPH NODES EXAMINED  1 Number of lymph nodes with metastases 0 02cm or less  isolated tumor cells   1   3 cells   Number of lymph nodes with metastases  0 02cm to 0 2cm  micrometastases   0 Number of lymph nodes with metastases  0 2cm  macrometastases   0 Method of detection  Cytokeratin immunohistochemistry  Extracapsular extension  None  Other forms of axillary involvement  None  LYMPH NODE  LEFT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY  1  INVASIVE CARCINOMA WITH DUCTAL AND LOBULAR FEATURES  SEE TABLE  2  2  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU AND CARCINOMA IN SITU WITH DUCTAL AND LOBULAR FEATURES  3  HEALING BIOPSY SITE  4  SEE NOTE  NOTE  The invasive carcinoma is essentially negative for E cadherin  The in situ carcinoma shows areas with ductal differentiation and other areas with a lobular like growth pattern  However  it is not clear that the two processes are distinct in situ lesions  Indeed  a morphologic spectrum between the two exists  favoring that they represent a related neoplastic process  Results of E cadherin stains in the in situ component are variable  there is strong positivity in some areas with ductal differentiation  only focal and very weak positivity in other areas with ductal differentiation  and negativity in areas with a lobular like growth pattern  Given the overall morphologic features and the fact that ductal carcinomas may lose E cadherin expression  these changes may simply represent biologic variability of a fundamentally ductal type neoplasm  However  to acknowledge the lobular like pattern of spread and minimal to absent E cadherin reactivity in some areas  both the invasive carcinoma and some of the in situ carcinoma are classified as having both ductal and lobular features  TABLE OF PATHOLOGICAL FINDINGS   2 INVASIVE CARCINOMA TUMOR SIZE  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm with a 0 12cm satellite nodule  based on combined gross and microscopic measurements   GRADE  2  LYMPHATIC VESSEL INVASION  Not identified  BLOOD VESSEL INVASION  Not identified  MARGIN OF INVASIVE CARCINOMA  The distances to all margins measure 0 2cm or greater  LOCATION OF CARCINOMA IN SITU  Within and beyond the region of the mass  GRADE OF CARCINOMA IN SITU  2 to 3  MARGIN OF CARCINOMA IN SITU  Carcinoma in situ focally extends to  0 1cm from the posterior margin  STAINS FOR RECEPTORS  Requested on block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   BREAST  left axilla   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm tan lymph node  The specimen is bisected and submitted entirely as FX 1  now as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN and  sentinel node hot and blue left breast   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm left breast simple mastectomy specimen which is partially surfaced by a REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm wrinkled white nipple areolar complex  There is a 0 6cm in di