Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  11 AUG 98 ACCESSIONED ON  11 AUG 98 at 10 35 CLINICAL DATA  Right breast cancer  biopsied elsewhere  reviewed here  Stitch is superior                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   MASTECTOMY  INVASIVE LOBULAR CARCINOMA  INTERMEDIATE GRADE  DIFFUSELY INFILTRATING THE BREAST  PRESENT IN ELEVEN OF FOURTEEN SLIDES  AND EXTENDING TO REMOVED_DATE CM FROM THE DEEP RESECTION MARGIN  LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLA   DISSECTION  METASTATIC CARCINOMA IN THIRTEEN OF THIRTEEN LYMPH NODES WITH MODERATE EXTRACAPSULAR TUMOR EXTENSION  Diagnosis by  EDI BROGI  MD  PhD Signed On  14 AUG 98 at 18 06                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  Right   The tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  04 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 14 33     HER 2 Addendum     RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR HER 2 c erb REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Breast  Right   The tumor cells show moderate overexpression of HER 2 c erb 2  See note  Note  This test was developed and its performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  It has not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  28 REMOVED_MONTH 99 at 14 07 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number only  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 5cm right modified radical mastectomy with a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm portion of attached axillary tail and a REMOVED_DATE x 4 9cm tan white skin ellipse  The skin ellipse has an eccentric 3 5cm unremarkable nipple areola complex  There is a 3 5cm horizontal  healing surgical incision on the lateral aspect of the skin ellipse located 0 5cm from the closest skin margin  superior margin   The specimen has a suture designating the superior aspect  Sectioning beneath the skin s scar reveals several small biopsy cavities  The first measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm and is hemorrhagic  This site is located 0 2cm from the skin margin and 2 5cm from the deep margin  The second identifiable site is located 0 8cm posteriorly from the first site and 1 3cm from the deep margin  Adjacent to the site is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 6cm firm  focally gray white mass which abuts the deep margin  Further sectioning reveals a