Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  26 REMOVED_MONTH 96 ACCESSIONED ON  26 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 11 02 CLINICAL DATA  Breast cancer  plus additional calcification  Needle core biopsy revealed infiltrating ductal carcinoma                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT  SPECIMEN DESIGNATED BY TWO SUTURES  PARTIAL MASTECTOMY   1  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  95    REMOVED_DATE CM  MODERATELY DIFFERENTIATED  EXTENDING TO THE ANTERIOR  SUPERFICIAL  RESECTION MARGIN  AND REMOVED_DATE CM FROM THE DEEP RESECTION MARGIN   SEE NOTE  2  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU   5   SOLID AND CRIBRIFORM TYPES WITH COMEDO TYPE NECROSIS  INTERMEDIATE GRADE  PRESENT AT THE ANTERIOR MARGIN AND LESS THAN REMOVED_DATE CM FROM THE DEEP MARGIN  3  RADIAL SCARS  4  COLLAGENOUS SPHENULOSIS  NOTE  Definite blood vascular invasion is not seen  The frozen section diagnosis is confirmed  BREAST   LEFT BREAST MASS    BIOPSY  1  ATYPICAL INTRADUCTAL HYPERPLASIA AT AN INKED SURFACE  2  RADIAL SCARS  3  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES WITH MICROCALCIFICATIONS  4  COLLAGENOUS SPHERULOSIS  BREAST  ADDITIONAL SUPERFICIAL MARGIN   EXCISION  BREAST PARENCHYMA WITH FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLARY   DISSECTION  METASTATIC CARCINOMA IN 6 OF 14 LYMPH NODES   SEE NOTE  NOTE  Extra nodal tumor extension is present in 3 of the 6 positive nodes  Peri nodal lymphatic involvement is seen  Diagnosis by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  28 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 19 03                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left  mass   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  01 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 15 07 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  are five parts  Received in the Frozen Section Lab  labeled  left breast mass  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm biopsy specimen with localizing wire in place and accompanying X ray film  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal scattered cystic structure ranging in size from REMOVED_DATE to 0 3cm  The specimen is submitted entirely in cassettes A through J  with area corresponding to calcification in cassettes A through D  Received in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast mass  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm lumpectomy specimen with a short stitch designating the superior margin and the long stitch designating the lateral margin  The specimen is inked entirely with black and additionally with yellow posteriorly  deep margin   and superiorly with red  The specimen is sectioned to reveal an ill defined REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm tan firm nodule present focally at the superficial  anterior  resection margin  0 5cm from the medial margin and 1 0cm from the deep resection margin  The remaining breast parenchyma is fibrous and focally cystic  K  tumor with superficial and deep resection margins L M andN  tumor with deep resection margin O  fibrous area with superficial and superior resection margins Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  additional superifical margin of breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm fragment of unoriented fibroadipose tissue which is inked and section  and submitted entirely in cassettes P and Q  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left axillary tissue contents  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm fibroadipose tissue  Lymph nodes are dissected and submitted in cassettes R and S  Received fresh  labeled  additional left axillary tissue  are two fragments of fibroadipose tissue  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm and each  and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm lymph node  The fibroadipose tissue fragments are submitted entirely in cassette T  The lymph node is bivalved and submitted in cassette Q  Resident  CHIN LEE WU  MD  PhD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  TUMOR PRESENT AT A SUPERFICIAL  ANTERIOR  MARGIN  O R  Resident  Timothy R  Quinn  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Eugene Jerome Mark  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  PART A  BREAST  LEFT   BIOPSY PART B  AXILLARY CONTENTS  LEFT  PART C  AXILLARY CONTENTS  LEFT  PART D  BREAST  LEFT SUPERFICIAL MARGIN  PART E  BREAST  LEFT   LUMPECTOMY   report_end  , Yes.
