en the 2 silver metal clips  No other gross abnormalities are identified  Representative sections are submitted from lateral to medial as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   with the lateral end en face as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   the medial end radially sectioned as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   the hemorrhagic area as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   and the tissue containing the probable previous biopsy site and 2 silver metal clips as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received fresh  labeled  right breast inferior   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 1cm portion of tan red fibrofatty tissue with a localization wire in place  A short black stitch designates the superior margin  and a long black stitch designates the lateral margin  The posterior margin is inked black  the anterior blue  the medial green  and the lateral yellow  The specimen is serially sectioned from superior to inferior to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 1cm well circumscribed gray white fibrous nodule which abuts the posterior and medial margins and comes to 0 3cm of the anterior  2 4cm of the lateral  1 2cm of the inferior  and  2cm from the superior margin  A silver metal clip is noted within the nodule  No other gross abnormalities are identified  Representative sections are submitted from superior to inferior as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   with the superior end en face as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   the inferior end en face as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   the entire nodule as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   and the tissue containing the metal clip as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  Tortolani  REMOVE_MRN   Right Superior   Excision PART B  Breast  Right Inferior   Excision PART C  Breast  , Yes.
